euthydemus-learn.logic.r3: argue/answered: U2: answered yes, which keeps euthydemus-learn.logic.r3.2 and euthydemus-learn.logic.r3.3, to: Does the text's argument take this for granted, whether or not it says so: "for every x, if x is wise, in the sense of already knowing what is being learned (S7), then x already knows the things x is learning"? Answer yes if the author would accept it as part of the argument.
